<SiteLayout title="Employee Attendance Software | Timenox | VYQDA" description="Explore Timenox browser-based employee attendance software for QR check-in and check-out, optional GPS and photo verification, shift scheduling and attendance reports." canonical="https://vyqda.com/products/timenox/" active="products">
<section class="page-hero"><div class="wrap page-hero__inner"><div class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><a href="/products/">Products</a><span>/</span><span>Timenox</span></div><p class="page-eyebrow">EMPLOYEE ATTENDANCE</p><h1>Employee attendance software built around the daily check-in.</h1><p class="page-hero__lead">Timenox is a browser-based attendance product for organisations that need a structured way for employees to check in and out and for managers to review attendance records.</p><div class="page-hero__actions"><a class="button button--primary" href="https://timenox.com/">Explore Timenox <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="button button--secondary" href="/contact/#project-enquiry">Discuss product fit</a></div></div></section>
<section class="content-section"><div class="wrap page-split"><div><p class="section-kicker">THE CORE JOB</p><h2>Make attendance capture easier to understand and manage.</h2><p>Timenox focuses on attendance rather than trying to describe every field-operation requirement. Employees use a browser-based flow to check in and out; organisations can evaluate options such as QR-based attendance, GPS and photo verification, shift scheduling and reports against their policies.</p><p>Confirm the available configuration, browser/device compatibility and data-handling details before rollout. The right setup depends on how your people work and what the organisation needs to record.</p></div><ol class="page-list"><li><span>01</span><div><strong>Define the attendance rule</strong><p>Decide who records attendance, which shifts apply and what constitutes a valid check-in or check-out.</p></div></li><li><span>02</span><div><strong>Choose proportionate verification</strong><p>Assess whether QR, location or photo checks are necessary for the attendance policy and explain the process to employees.</p></div></li><li><span>03</span><div><strong>Prepare schedules and reports</strong><p>List the shift patterns, exceptions and summaries managers need to review.</p></div></li><li><span>04</span><div><strong>Test real devices</strong><p>Check the employee journey on the browsers and phones your team actually uses.</p></div></li></ol></div></section>
<section class="content-section content-section--tint"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-heading-page"><p class="section-kicker">PRODUCT FIT</p><h2>When should you evaluate Timenox?</h2><p>It is worth evaluating when your main problem is recording and reviewing employee attendance—not managing a wider sequence of field visits or operational tasks.</p></div><div class="page-grid"><article class="page-card"><span class="page-card__number">01</span><h3>Office and on-site teams</h3><p>You need a repeatable check-in and check-out process for people reporting to a workplace.</p></article><article class="page-card"><span class="page-card__number">02</span><h3>Shift-based organisations</h3><p>You need to consider schedules and attendance summaries as part of everyday workforce administration.</p></article><article class="page-card"><span class="page-card__number">03</span><h3>Teams moving from informal records</h3><p>You want to assess a structured browser-based workflow rather than relying only on manual registers or messages.</p></article></div></div></section>
<section class="content-section"><div class="wrap page-split"><div><p class="section-kicker">EVALUATION CHECKLIST</p><h2>Questions to settle before choosing attendance software.</h2><p>Use these criteria to assess product fit. They are evaluation questions, not a claim that every possible workflow is supported.</p></div><ol class="page-list"><li><span>01</span><div><strong>Employee onboarding</strong><p>How are employees identified and shown the correct check-in process?</p></div></li><li><span>02</span><div><strong>Exceptions and missed punches</strong><p>What should happen when someone forgets to check out or cannot access a device?</p></div></li><li><span>03</span><div><strong>Privacy and access</strong><p>Who can see attendance data, and when are location or photo checks justified?</p></div></li><li><span>04</span><div><strong>Reports and export needs</strong><p>Confirm the actual reports and data formats available for your use case.</p></div></li></ol></div></section>
<section class="content-section content-section--tint"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-heading-page"><p class="section-kicker">CHOOSING BETWEEN PRODUCTS</p><h2>Timenox or Timenox 360?</h2><p>Start with the operational job. <strong>Timenox</strong> is the more relevant starting point when the central need is employee attendance capture and attendance records. <strong><a href="/products/timenox-360/">Timenox 360</a></strong> is positioned for field-team and distributed operations workflows. Do not assume continuous location tracking or any specific field feature without confirming the current product specification.</p><a class="page-text-link" href="/products/timenox-360/">Explore Timenox 360 <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></div></section>
<section class="content-section product-faq-section"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-heading-page"><p class="section-kicker">COMMON QUESTIONS</p><h2>About Timenox attendance software</h2></div><div class="faq-page-list"><details><summary>Is Timenox browser-based?</summary><p>Yes. Timenox is a browser-based attendance product. Validate supported browsers and devices used by your employees before rollout.</p></details><details><summary>Does Timenox support GPS and photo verification?</summary><p>GPS and photo verification options are part of the described Timenox workflow. Confirm availability and configuration for your intended plan and deployment.</p></details><details><summary>Is Timenox designed for continuous field tracking?</summary><p>This page positions Timenox around attendance check-in and check-out. If your main requirement is broader field operations, evaluate Timenox 360 and confirm its current location-capture behaviour directly.</p></details><details><summary>What should we prepare before a product discussion?</summary><p>Bring employee and shift patterns, check-in locations, device expectations, reporting requirements and any privacy or data-retention constraints.</p></details></div></div></section>
